{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישב על פי החירות", :translit "vayashav al pi hachirot", :gloss "and he turned toward Pi HaChirot"} {:he "ואינו אומר וישובו", :translit "ve'eino omer veyashvu", :gloss "and it does not say 'and they turned'"} {:he "מלמד שכולם היה להם לב אחד לעשות כן ע\"פ ציווי של משה", :translit "melamed shekulam hayah lahem lev echad la'asot ken al pi tzivui shel moshe", :gloss "teaching that all of them had one heart to do so, by command of Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Singular verb וישב instead of plural וישובו implies collective unity of action"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "על פי החירות", :translit "al pi hachirot", :gloss "toward Pi HaChirot"} {:he "לפני פי החירות", :translit "lifnei pi hachirot", :gloss "before Pi HaChirot"} {:he "מלמד שאמר להם משה ע\"פ ה' אני אומר לכם שתהיו בני חורין", :translit "melamed she'amar lahem moshe al pi hashem ani omer lachem she tihyu bnei chorin", :gloss "teaching that Moses said to them: by word of YHWH I say to you that you shall be free men"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name פי החירות read as 'mouth of freedom,' paired with change from על to לפני in Exodus 14:2"}], :frame {:text "In Exodus 14:2 the Israelites are commanded to encamp לפני פי החירות, 'before Pi HaChirot' (Exodus 14:2), whereas here in Numbers 33:7 the phrasing is על פי החירות. The name פי החירות is read as 'mouth of freedom,' signaling that at this location Israel received the divine guarantee of liberation — בני חורין, 'free men' (Exodus 14:2, Exodus 13:18).", :sources ["Exodus 14:2" "Exodus 13:18" "Numbers 33:7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Singular verb וישב instead of plural וישובו implies collective unity of action", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Place-name פי החירות read as 'mouth of freedom,' paired with change from על to לפני in Exodus 14:2", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-